Part d (5 points)
Based on what we learned in Part c, create a new variable in our data frame that represents “normalized” or “standardized” estimates of the added sugars in a “serving” of cereal. This variable should be named sugars_weight and should represent the total number of sugars per unit of Weight. Note that Weight is a standardized measure that represents the relative weight of a typical serving of cereal. It does not represent ounces, or grams, or other typical measurements of weight. Normally, we would say “total number of sugars per ounce” or “sugars per gram”. But, because of the way our measurements were taken, all we can say about this new variable is “sugars per unit of weight.”
Note that you must use the mutate() function from the tidyverse to add this variable to your dataframe. Then, using the same tidyverse pipe, calculate the average number of sugars per unit of weight using the variable you have created and assign that value to the variable sugars_weight_mean. Ensure that the provided code prints TRUE when you are finished.


